{"type":"document","version":"0.2","doc":"format_x_rulebook","source":"format_x_rulebook_v0.2.md","sha256":"fde4f7b3692426a01d6e8a028cdae43a504a3bb52e3d625e896b2185649ab796","protection":"none","signed":false,"converter":"fmjl 0.2","structure":true,"elements":64,"created":"2026-09-26T11:05:28Z","lang":"en","access":["all"]}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e1","hash":"bb3afb4cdf1e5831","type":"heading","level":1,"parent":null,"characters":32,"md":"# Format X Rulebook, Version 0.2"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e2","hash":"a9e99a7a32403d87","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":98,"md":"Status: draft. Format X files use the extension `.fmjl`. The name and license are not decided yet."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e3","hash":"901c32301e60606d","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 1. What Format X Is"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e4","hash":"da54cb8df3169ea9","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e3","characters":177,"md":"Format X stores any document as a list of small parts called elements, one element per line. It is built for RAG systems that need accuracy, speed, and context at the same time."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e5","hash":"92870383050dddab","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e3","characters":33,"md":"Format X combines four languages:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e6","hash":"c5d09219dce34072","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e3","characters":298,"md":"| Language | Role | Where it appears |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| JSON (JSON Lines) | The container: one JSON object per line | Every line |\n| Markdown | All readable text | The `md` field |\n| LaTeX | Raw math formulas | The `latex` field |\n| HTML | Complex tables with merged cells | The `html` field |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e7","hash":"d3f4b2259a34558f","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e3","characters":38,"md":"Three rules make sure nothing is lost:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e8","hash":"882fe5a870aef09c","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e3","characters":307,"md":"1. Every part of the original document becomes an element, including stamps, logos, watermarks, and blacked-out areas.\n2. Every element from a page-based file records its page and position, so its exact spot in the original can always be found.\n3. The original file is always kept next to the Format X file."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e9","hash":"e4f544d77b10ca08","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":20,"md":"## 2. Storage Layout"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e10","hash":"465c13b2d1101a2a","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":56,"md":"While processing, each document is stored as one folder:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e11","hash":"ecfd49226a84de86","type":"code","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":171,"md":"```text\nleave_policy/\n  leave_policy.fmjl     the Format X file\n  images/               cropped images, PNG or WebP\n  original/             the untouched original file\n```"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e12","hash":"bed734740a4238b7","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":57,"md":"For sharing, the same folder is packed into one zip file."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e13","hash":"46529d547e782a85","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":175,"md":"The file extension is `.fmjl`, short for Format, Markdown, JSON Lines. Inside, an `.fmjl` file is plain JSON Lines, so any JSON Lines tool or programming language can read it."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e14","hash":"3d8cc7626a92d8aa","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":11,"md":"File rules:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e15","hash":"c5ee3df4fa7d7d6f","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e9","characters":246,"md":"1. Text encoding is UTF-8.\n2. Each line is exactly one JSON object. Lines end with a newline character, and there are no empty lines.\n3. Line 1 is the header line. Every following line is an element line.\n4. Element lines appear in reading order."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e16","hash":"c1709179f0c14f69","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":21,"md":"## 3. The Header Line"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e17","hash":"cd54c445ff0dceee","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e16","characters":122,"md":"The header line describes the whole document. It has `\"type\": \"document\"` and all 12 fields below, which are all required."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e18","hash":"14e5dbff0971865b","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e16","characters":1085,"md":"| Field | Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `version` | Text | The rulebook version the file follows, for example `\"0.1\"` |\n| `doc` | Text | Short document name, using lowercase letters, digits, `_` or `-` |\n| `source` | Text | The original file name |\n| `sha256` | 64 hexadecimal characters | Fingerprint of the original file, used to skip duplicate uploads |\n| `protection` | `none`, `password`, `certificate`, or `drm` | How the original file was locked |\n| `signed` | `true` or `false` | Whether the original carries a digital signature |\n| `converter` | Text | The tool and version that created this file |\n| `structure` | `true` or `false` | `false` means no headings were found, so the file should be converted again with a better tool |\n| `elements` | Whole number | The number of element lines in the file |\n| `created` | Date and time (ISO 8601, UTC) | When the file was created |\n| `lang` | Language code | The main language, for example `\"en\"`, `\"hi\"`, `\"as\"`, or `\"bn\"` |\n| `access` | List of group names | The default permission, for example `[\"all\"]` or `[\"hr\"]` |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e19","hash":"85ef44ab2c5e654d","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e16","characters":119,"md":"Security rule: `protection` records only how a file was locked. A password or key is never stored anywhere in Format X."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e20","hash":"f114c436f8b2be7e","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 4. Element Lines"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e21","hash":"92eba19537e6eda2","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e20","characters":23,"md":"### 4.1 Required Fields"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e22","hash":"072a0f5abef830aa","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e21","characters":38,"md":"Every element line has these 6 fields:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e23","hash":"341746c991c29eb8","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e21","characters":545,"md":"| Field | Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | Text | `<doc>#e<number>`, numbered from 1 in reading order, for example `leave_policy#e7` |\n| `hash` | 16 hexadecimal characters | Content fingerprint, defined in section 6.1 |\n| `type` | One of the 19 types | What kind of part this is, defined in section 5 |\n| `parent` | Element ID or `null` | The nearest heading above with a lower level, or `null` if there is none |\n| `characters` | Whole number | The number of characters in `md` |\n| `md` | Text | The content, written in Markdown |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e24","hash":"e10b05a74340a61b","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e20","characters":23,"md":"### 4.2 Optional Fields"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e25","hash":"cd7e3eb1462d4b8b","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e24","characters":953,"md":"| Field | Value | Used when |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `subtype` | Text | The element is an `image` or `noise` |\n| `level` | 1 to 6 | The element is a `heading` (required for headings) |\n| `page` | Whole number, from 0 | The element sits on one page |\n| `pages` | List of page numbers | The element spans several pages, like a long table |\n| `bbox` | `[left, top, right, bottom]` | The position on the page is known |\n| `reference` | Element ID, or a list of IDs | The element points to other elements |\n| `confidence` | Number from 0 to 1 | The content came from OCR or an AI model |\n| `lang` | Language code | The element's language differs from the header |\n| `access` | List of group names | The element's permission differs from the header |\n| `html` | Text | A `table` has merged cells or multi-level headers |\n| `latex` | Text | The element is a `formula` (required for formulas) |\n| `file` | Path | The element is an `image` (required for images) |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e26","hash":"6d181716592a4cc8","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e24","characters":154,"md":"When an optional field is missing, a default applies: no `confidence` means fully certain (1), and no `lang` or `access` means the header's value applies."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e27","hash":"e970849af143a1fb","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 5. Element Types"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e28","hash":"fa95ecf9b4cea238","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e27","characters":1659,"md":"| # | Type | Holds | Rules |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `heading` | Titles and subtitles | Needs `level` |\n| 2 | `paragraph` | Normal text | Inline formulas stay in `md` as `$...$` |\n| 3 | `list` | Bullet or numbered points | The whole list is one element |\n| 4 | `table` | Rows and columns | Never split; may add `html` |\n| 5 | `formula` | Display math | Needs `latex`; `md` holds `$$...$$` |\n| 6 | `code` | Program code | `md` is a fenced code block that names the language |\n| 7 | `image` | Pictures, charts, logos, stamps, signatures, QR codes | Needs `file`; `md` holds a text description |\n| 8 | `caption` | The label of a table or image | `reference` points to that table or image |\n| 9 | `footnote` | Notes at the bottom of a page | `reference` points to the text that uses it |\n| 10 | `form_field` | Form entries and checkboxes | `md` looks like `- [x] Married` |\n| 11 | `annotation` | Comments and handwritten notes | Usually has `confidence` |\n| 12 | `redaction` | Blacked-out hidden parts | `md` is `[REDACTED]` |\n| 13 | `noise` | Page headers, footers, watermarks, page numbers | Needs `subtype`; kept but not searched |\n| 14 | `message` | One email or chat message | Sender and date go at the top of `md` |\n| 15 | `utterance` | One speaker's turn in a transcript | Speaker and time go at the top of `md` |\n| 16 | `record` | One CSV row or one JSON object | `md` lists the fields as `Name: value` |\n| 17 | `citation` | A reference or bibliography entry | In-text markers link here with `reference` |\n| 18 | `quote` | Quoted text from another source | `md` uses `>` |\n| 19 | `toc` | A table of contents | Kept for structure but not searched |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e29","hash":"cc154e12ad3504cd","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e27","characters":9,"md":"Subtypes:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e30","hash":"5d40d47ef2c0f572","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e27","characters":230,"md":"1. For `image`: `logo`, `stamp`, `signature`, `chart`, `diagram`, `photo`, `qr_code`, or `barcode`. For `qr_code` and `barcode`, `md` also holds the decoded value.\n2. For `noise`: `header`, `footer`, `watermark`, or `page_number`."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e31","hash":"ea7405f48b7f3158","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":17,"md":"## 6. Field Rules"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e32","hash":"713f6c7a0c1e2877","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e31","characters":12,"md":"### 6.1 Hash"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e33","hash":"2a0499e914e51ce6","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e32","characters":211,"md":"`hash` is the first 16 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 of the text `type`, a newline, then `md`, encoded in UTF-8. When a document is uploaded again, only elements whose `hash` changed need new embeddings."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e34","hash":"e6cc897fae6de718","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e31","characters":27,"md":"### 6.2 Pages and Positions"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e35","hash":"5c389e4a2d02c54b","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e34","characters":455,"md":"1. Page numbers start at 0. When showing a page number to users, add 1.\n2. An element has `page` or `pages`, never both. `pages` holds at least two numbers, in order.\n3. `bbox` is `[left, top, right, bottom]` in whole numbers from 0 to 1000, where 1000 is the full page width or height and `[0, 0]` is the top-left corner.\n4. `bbox` is allowed only together with `page`.\n5. For slides, `page` is the slide number. For spreadsheets, it is the sheet number."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e36","hash":"4a3eb67c1dbe0741","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e31","characters":28,"md":"### 6.3 Allowed Combinations"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e37","hash":"fe8fcf2587ff5bd4","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e36","characters":230,"md":"1. `md` follows CommonMark, plus GitHub-style tables, strikethrough, and task lists.\n2. `html` is allowed only on `table`, `latex` only on `formula`, and `file` only on `image`.\n3. `subtype` is allowed only on `image` and `noise`."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e38","hash":"39d5a8631cbdaa3e","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 7. Input Formats"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e39","hash":"de498a67fd5e8980","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e38","characters":45,"md":"Format X accepts all formats, in five groups:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e40","hash":"2cb3099fa4cf46c8","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e38","characters":747,"md":"| Group | Formats | How they are converted |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Page-based | PDF, TIFF, PNG, JPG, and other scans | Full pipeline with OCR and layout detection; fills `page`, `bbox`, and `confidence` |\n| Structured | DOCX, DOC, PPTX, ODT, RTF, HTML, Markdown, EPUB, LaTeX | Structure is read directly, with no OCR |\n| Tables | XLSX, XLS, ODS, CSV, TSV | Sheets become `table` elements split by rows, with the header row repeated; CSV rows become `record` elements |\n| Code and data | Source code, JSON, JSONL, YAML, XML | Code becomes one `code` element per function or class; data becomes one `record` per object |\n| Email and transcripts | EML, MSG, MBOX, chat exports, SRT, VTT | One `message` per message; one `utterance` per speaker turn |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e41","hash":"d4c8369cb0510b58","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e38","characters":98,"md":"TIFF and other image formats are accepted as input only. Images saved by Format X use PNG or WebP."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e42","hash":"295a653021dddd19","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 8. Processing Order"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e43","hash":"2f2207c8a30bf4d6","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e42","characters":485,"md":"1. Quick check: confirm the file is valid, not a duplicate (`sha256`), which pages are digital or scanned, the language, and the page count.\n2. Convert: extract every part into elements and write the file.\n3. Final check: run the checks listed below.\n4. Chunk: pack elements into chunks by `characters`. Elements are never split, except a paragraph or list longer than one chunk, which is split at sentence boundaries.\n5. Embed: create embeddings and store them in the vector database."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e44","hash":"5dd122c5586ffa1b","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e42","characters":77,"md":"If the final check fails, convert again with a stronger tool and check again."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e45","hash":"db3a1c1abdef5bc4","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e42","characters":30,"md":"The final check confirms that:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e46","hash":"565d679fc73169c1","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e42","characters":350,"md":"1. The number of element lines equals `elements` in the header.\n2. Every line passes the JSON Schema in section 11.\n3. Every `parent` and `reference` points to an existing element.\n4. Every `file` exists in the `images/` folder.\n5. Every `hash` and `characters` value matches its `md`.\n6. `structure` is `true`, or the document truly has no headings."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e47","hash":"4b244af99eee5ec4","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":21,"md":"## 9. Retrieval Rules"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e48","hash":"d78309c17d2a4236","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e47","characters":508,"md":"1. Filter by `access` before searching, so users never see parts they are not allowed to see.\n2. Do not embed `noise`, `toc`, or `redaction` elements.\n3. Rebuild each element's section path from its `parent` chain, and add it to the chunk for context.\n4. Return `caption` and `citation` elements together with the elements they reference.\n5. When an answer uses content with low `confidence`, show the original region using `page` and `bbox`.\n6. Cite answers with the element `id` and the page number plus 1."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e49","hash":"ed1f472772aeb03c","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 10. Reader Rules"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e50","hash":"27426ef6832d534f","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e49","characters":181,"md":"1. Readers ignore fields they do not know, so newer files stay readable.\n2. Readers treat unknown types as `paragraph`.\n3. A reader for version 0.x can read any file of version 0.x."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e51","hash":"56311afffc7bc177","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":18,"md":"## 11. JSON Schema"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e52","hash":"1ad9c490fd4ac6bc","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e51","characters":147,"md":"This schema checks every line automatically (JSON Schema draft 2020-12). A line is valid if it matches either the header or the element definition."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e53","hash":"3acb266e77b0d953","type":"code","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e51","characters":8170,"md":"```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"Format X (.fmjl) line, version 0.2\",\n  \"oneOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/header\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/element\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"header\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"version\",\n        \"doc\",\n        \"source\",\n        \"sha256\",\n        \"protection\",\n        \"signed\",\n        \"converter\",\n        \"structure\",\n        \"elements\",\n        \"created\",\n        \"lang\",\n        \"access\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"document\"\n        },\n        \"version\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+$\"\n        },\n        \"doc\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+$\"\n        },\n        \"source\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\"\n        },\n        \"protection\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"none\",\n            \"password\",\n            \"certificate\",\n            \"drm\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"signed\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"converter\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"structure\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"elements\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"created\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"format\": \"date-time\"\n        },\n        \"lang\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)*$\"\n        },\n        \"access\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"element\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"id\",\n        \"hash\",\n        \"type\",\n        \"parent\",\n        \"characters\",\n        \"md\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n        },\n        \"hash\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{16}$\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"heading\",\n            \"paragraph\",\n            \"list\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"formula\",\n            \"code\",\n            \"image\",\n            \"caption\",\n            \"footnote\",\n            \"form_field\",\n            \"annotation\",\n            \"redaction\",\n            \"noise\",\n            \"message\",\n            \"utterance\",\n            \"record\",\n            \"citation\",\n            \"quote\",\n            \"toc\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"subtype\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"level\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 6\n        },\n        \"parent\": {\n          \"type\": [\n            \"string\",\n            \"null\"\n          ],\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n        },\n        \"page\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"pages\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"bbox\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 4,\n          \"maxItems\": 4,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 0,\n            \"maximum\": 1000\n          }\n        },\n        \"characters\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"reference\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"minItems\": 1,\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n              }\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"confidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\",\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"maximum\": 1\n        },\n        \"lang\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)*$\"\n        },\n        \"access\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"html\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"latex\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^images/[^/]+\\\\.(png|webp)$\"\n        },\n        \"md\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"bbox\": [\n          \"page\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"not\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"page\",\n          \"pages\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"allOf\": [\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"heading\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"level\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"formula\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"latex\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"image\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"file\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"subtype\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"logo\",\n                  \"stamp\",\n                  \"signature\",\n                  \"chart\",\n                  \"diagram\",\n                  \"photo\",\n                  \"qr_code\",\n                  \"barcode\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"noise\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"subtype\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"subtype\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"header\",\n                  \"footer\",\n                  \"watermark\",\n                  \"page_number\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"level\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"heading\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"html\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"table\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"latex\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"formula\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"file\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"image\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"subtype\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"image\",\n                  \"noise\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e54","hash":"fe82e689914ce4cf","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":14,"md":"## 12. Example"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e55","hash":"1cc68e5cc1f8841e","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e54","characters":60,"md":"A complete, valid `.fmjl` file for a short leave policy PDF:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e56","hash":"496083e8dfdb6113","type":"code","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e54","characters":1626,"md":"```json\n{\"type\":\"document\",\"version\":\"0.2\",\"doc\":\"leave_policy\",\"source\":\"leave_policy.pdf\",\"sha256\":\"af179a761f988e6a40d5154b3c3ce735ba94d23ebd82d8e24e3d80de4e2dda68\",\"protection\":\"none\",\"signed\":false,\"converter\":\"docling 2.x\",\"structure\":true,\"elements\":6,\"created\":\"2026-09-25T10:30:00Z\",\"lang\":\"en\",\"access\":[\"all\"]}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"hash\":\"b323ab53d73b48e7\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":1,\"parent\":null,\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,60,620,95],\"characters\":14,\"md\":\"# Leave Policy\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e2\",\"hash\":\"8d92bcc782e5c0ca\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,110,920,170],\"characters\":76,\"md\":\"This policy applies to all full-time employees from their first day of work.\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e3\",\"hash\":\"79e15a433bf84d1c\",\"type\":\"table\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,190,700,330],\"characters\":89,\"md\":\"| Leave type | Days per year |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Sick leave | 12 |\\n| Paternity leave | 15 |\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e4\",\"hash\":\"fd6cd4502fca6a4a\",\"type\":\"caption\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,335,400,355],\"characters\":20,\"reference\":\"leave_policy#e3\",\"md\":\"Table 1: Leave types\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e5\",\"hash\":\"8f843b2362f0d607\",\"type\":\"image\",\"subtype\":\"stamp\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[700,820,900,940],\"characters\":66,\"confidence\":0.91,\"file\":\"images/leave_policy_e5.png\",\"md\":\"Round blue stamp reading \\\"Brightpath Technologies, HR Department\\\".\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e6\",\"hash\":\"731af9f7a14feaf5\",\"type\":\"noise\",\"subtype\":\"footer\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[460,960,540,980],\"characters\":6,\"md\":\"Page 1\"}\n```"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e57","hash":"4da28b7975113d2a","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":12,"md":"## 13. Tools"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e58","hash":"fa54d8d9050acbc2","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e57","characters":47,"md":"The reference tool `fmjl.py` has four commands:"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e59","hash":"e414572d3368a93b","type":"table","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e57","characters":426,"md":"| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `python fmjl.py new notes.md --doc my_notes` | Converts a Markdown file into `my_notes.fmjl` |\n| `python fmjl.py fill my_notes.fmjl` | Fills in `id`, `hash`, `characters`, `parent`, and the header counts |\n| `python fmjl.py check my_notes.fmjl` | Checks every rule and prints errors with line numbers |\n| `python fmjl.py view my_notes.fmjl` | Prints the file as a readable document |"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e60","hash":"a6c7edb9ce5a9dfe","type":"paragraph","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e57","characters":146,"md":"It needs Python and two packages: `pip install markdown-it-py jsonschema`. A file is valid only if `check` passes, whatever any person or AI says."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e61","hash":"6305ccb85a0d9ff8","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 14. Version History"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e62","hash":"59c4e5779c4cb691","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e61","characters":140,"md":"1. Version 0.1: first draft, with the extension `.jsonl`.\n2. Version 0.2: the extension `.fmjl` is decided, and the `fmjl.py` tool is added."}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e63","hash":"f8d2d11c846b2049","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"format_x_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 15. Not Decided Yet"}
{"id":"format_x_rulebook#e64","hash":"fd9ab63fba79029d","type":"list","parent":"format_x_rulebook#e63","characters":64,"md":"1. The format name. \"Format X\" is a placeholder.\n2. The license."}
